> Why do you think wishless is easier with a wizard?

In my opinion the one thing that is absolutely essential for an
ascension is magic resistance. Wizards start with it. 

Also, a wizard can obtain a missing item more easily than the other
classes, as a bit patience coupled with either a cursed scroll of
genocide or a wand of undead turning can be used at the quest bottom
to obtain the spellbook of polymorph. With the eye and polymorph you
have a reasonable change of obtaining the ascension kit before being
killed by boredom.

Finally, a wizard does not have to use wishes for magic markers to
prepare for Gehennom, as they can easily cast magic mapping as often
as needed. This is the reason why the vast majority of my ascensions
are not wishless: I don't have the patience to traverse Gehennom
without magic mapping and I rarely find enough magic markers to map it
completely.

